},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The random priorities make the shape that of a random binary search tree, whatever order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements arrive in, so lookup, insertion and removal take O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") expected time. A treap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also splits at an element into the elements below it and the rest, and joins two treaps whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements don’t interleave. The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed by rank like an array: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"treap[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The priorities come from a random number generator given at creation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator"},{"type":"text","text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The treap draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"priorities as its original."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" links, so the treap holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/treap"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/Treap/max()":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/treap\/max()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"max"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/max()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The largest element, or nil when empty. O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":") expected.","type":"text"}],"title":"max()"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/Sl":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","title":"Swift.Collection"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/Treap/remove(checkedAt:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"remove"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"checkedAt"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16CollectionErrors15IndexOutOfRangeV","text":"IndexOutOfRange"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentati